BT /F2 13 Tf 44.0 487.0 Td (Executive Summary) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56.0 467.0 Td (- The existing Flask, LangGraph, and MongoDB HR agent system was hardened without replacing the product) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56.0 454.0 Td (workflow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56.0 439.0 Td (- The implementation adds typed validation, a policy-enforced tool gateway, tamper-evident audit logging, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56.0 426.0 Td (prompt/context safety checks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56.0 411.0 Td (- The core recruitment graph remains intact: router, screening path, recruiter chat path, and app workflow path) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56.0 398.0 Td (still use the same API surface.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56.0 383.0 Td (- Controlled mutations now have a security boundary instead of being called directly from agents or workflows.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 44.0 360.0 Td (Design Intent) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56.0 340.0 Td (- Preserve working HR behavior while adding production safeguards around the riskiest operations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56.0 325.0 Td (- Prefer incremental hardening over a disruptive migration to FastAPI, MCP servers, or a new database stack.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 56.0 310.0 Td (- Make unsafe or ambiguous actions fail closed with clear approval-required or authorization-denied responses.) Tj ET
q 0.7 w 44.0 34.0 m 798.0 34.0 l S Q
BT /F1 7 Tf 44.0 19.0 Td (RecruitmentAssist - Production Hardening Report) Tj ET
BT /F1 7 Tf 756.0 19.0 Td (Page 1) Tj ET
endstream
